 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a preview sheet is admitted to the cache, the system SHALL place it in Q1 (the short-term FIFO admission queue).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a cache request hits an entry held in Q1, the system SHALL promote that entry to the head of Qm (the main LRU queue) before serving the JPEG.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a cache request hits an entry held in Qm, the system SHALL move that entry to Qm's head before serving the JPEG.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When admitting a new sheet, the system SHALL evict entries from Q1's tail, then from Qm's tail if Q1 is empty, until the sheet fits within both the Q1 byte budget and the 12 GiB total cache budget.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: The cache SHALL enforce a configurable Q1 byte budget (default 20% of the 12 GiB total cache budget, ~2.4 GiB) set at startup; the Q1 budget SHALL be configured to at least one maximum sheet size.
